            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Quadrilaterals"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.54,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": "As opposite sides are parallel, GAME is also a parallelogram. Thus, every rhombus is a parallelogram, and the properties of a parallelogram hold true for a rhombus as well. Thus, the adjacent angles of a rhombus add up to 180°, and the opposite angles are equal if h h i D d i 6 can be applied to a rhombus (ver y t at t e arguments n e uct on as we !) ll ."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.547,
            0.092,
            0.846,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.253,
            0.419,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "Thus, in rhombus ABCD,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.404,
            0.277,
            0.596,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{C} = 50^{\\circ},  and",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.3,
            0.63,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{D} = \\angle \\mathrm{B} = 180 - 50 = 130^{\\circ}.",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.337,
            0.847,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": "? So a rhombus is a parallelogram, and a rectangle is also a parallelogram. How can this be represented using a Venn diagram?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.391,
            0.672,
            0.414
          ],
          "content": "？ Where will the set of squares occur in this diagram?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.416,
            0.848,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": "We know that a square is a rectangle. Since the opposite sides of a square are parallel, a square is also a parallelogram. Further, since all the sides of a square have the same length, a square is also a rhombus. Thus, the Venn diagram will be as follows."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.496,
            0.903,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.717,
            0.532,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "Let us list the properties of a rhombus."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.741,
            0.761,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": "**Property 1:** All the sides of a rhombus are equal to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.766,
            0.843,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": "**Property 2:** The opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.791,
            0.848,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "**Property 3:** In a rhombus, the adjacent angles add up to 180°, and the opposite angles are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.839,
            0.54,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "？ Are the diagonals of a rhombus equal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.87,
            0.72,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "**Property 4:** The diagonals of a rhombus bisect each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.895,
            0.71,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": "**Property 5:** The diagonals of a rhombus bisect its angles."
        },
        {
